   141	## 4. The BAND LEMMA and the MASTER theorem
   142	
   143	### 4.1 The band lemma
   144	
   145	> **BAND LEMMA.** Let `J(f,g) = c x^k`, `c ≠ 0`, `lf(f) = H²`, `lf(g) = H³`, and
   146	> let `Φ ∈ k[f,g]` with `Φ_g ≠ 0`, `Φ(f,g) ≠ 0`, `D := deg Φ(f,g)`. Then
   147	> ```
   148	>            k + deg Phi_g(f,g)   <=   2K + D - 2 ,
   149	> ```
   150	> with **equality iff** `J(H, Φ_D) ≠ 0`;
   151	> and if `J(H,Φ_D) = 0` then `K ∣ D` and `Φ_D = λH^{D/K}` with `λ ≠ 0`.
   152	>
   153	> *Proof.* `J(f, Φ(f,g)) = Φ_g(f,g)·J(f,g) = c x^k Φ_g(f,g)`, of degree
   154	> `k + deg Φ_g(f,g)`. On the other side `deg J(f,Φ) ≤ deg f + D − 2` with leading
   155	> form `J(H², Φ_D) = 2H·J(H,Φ_D)`. The last clause is LEMMA BF applied to
   156	> `(H, Φ_D)` exactly as in LEMMA INJ. ∎
   157	
   158	Applied to `Φ = g²−f³` (so `Φ_g = 2g`, `deg Φ_g(f,g) = 3K`) with `k = 4`:
