codex
The first raw recurrence screen did not decide the row: K=8 prefixes through \(q_2\) are modular positive-dimensional, while the \(q_3\) and terminal prefixes timed out at 45 seconds in all three primes. That is diagnostic rather than a verdict. I’ve moved the screen onto the closed parametrization, which removes the first two quotient bands and the entire next \(h\)-band before Gröbner reduction; the exact remainder-matching lane is proceeding independently.
