    35	## 1. Chart actually built
    36	
    37	Driver: `box/k4raypinned-20260903/pinned_chart.py`.
    38	
    39	The driver imports `box.lib.guided_gb` and uses `SingularSystem`,
    40	`RunConfig`, `PromotionPolicy.exact_q`, `HilbertHint`, and `guided_groebner`.
    41	The `guided_gb` wrapper runs Singular through `stdbuf -oL -eL`; the row-count
    42	prelude runner also uses `stdbuf`.
    43	
    44	The chart uses the charged normalization
    45	
    46	```text
    47	H = y^(K-1)(y-x)
    48	h = H + lower terms, monic in y
    49	B = 2 beta
    50	f = h^2 + B
    51	Al = quo_y(B^2,h) = 4 alpha
    52	Rh = B^2 - Al*h = 4 rho
    53	g = h^3 + (3/2) B h + (3/8) Al
    54	J = (3/8) J(B,Al) - (3/4) J(h,Rh)       (ID6)
    55	```
    56	
    57	For the residual bottom band the LEVEL-4 pin is imposed as
    58	
    59	```text
    60	beta_b = mu*y^(K-3)*(y-x),     b = K-2
    61	Btop  = 2*mu*y^(K-3)*(y-x)
    62	```
    63	
    64	The lower `B_i_j` variables are coefficients of `B=2 beta`, not of beta
    65	itself. This is only a scale convention; the named scalar `mu` is the beta top
    66	coefficient.
    67	
    68	The light decision ideal is
    69	
    70	```text
    71	I_light =
    72	  < all non-x^4 coefficients of J,
    73	    coeffs of Rh - (4/3)*mu^3*y^(K-7)*(y-x) in degrees >= K-6,
    74	    CSTP - 1,
    75	    mu*mu_inv - 1 >
    76	```
    77	
    78	where the rho rows combine the degree consequence `deg Rh <= K-6` with the
    79	LEVEL-4 top formula
    80	
    81	```text
    82	rho_(K-6) = beta_b^3 / (3 H^2).
    83	```
    84	
    85	This is a weaker ideal than the full theorem-cut ideal because it omits the
    86	additional rows from `deg(64*(g^2-f^3) - lambda*f) <= K+6`. Thus a unit ideal
    87	for `I_light` is a valid kill for the full theorem-valid chart: any larger
    88	ideal containing a unit ideal is also the unit ideal.
    89	
    90	The full theorem-cut variant additionally introduces `lambda` and adds all
    91	coefficients of
    92	
    93	```text
    94	E64lam = 8*B^3 - 48*Rh*h^2 - 72*B*Rh + 9*Al^2 - lambda*f
    95	```
    96	
    97	whose `x,y` degree is strictly larger than `K+6`. Coefficients are extracted
    98	with `coef(...,x*y)` and tested by `deg` on the displayed `x,y` monomial. This
    99	avoids the old `jet()` pitfall where parameter variables are counted in the
   100	degree.
   101	
   102	Ring map:
   103	
   104	```text
   105	RR = Q,(x,y,parameters),dp
   106	SS = Q,(parameters),wp(weights)
   107	ROWS = imap(RR,I0)
   108	CSTP = imap(RR,CST)
   109	```
   110	
   111	The charts are dehomogenized and localized by `CSTP-1` and `mu*mu_inv-1`.
   112	Accordingly, no homogeneous properness promotion is used for the main rows.
   113	Exact Q is the only characteristic-zero promotion path. Modular runs below are
   114	typed F_p-only diagnostics.
