   332	the beta recurrence: its positive bands equal `48Rh`, its scalar band equals
   333	`48Rh_0+lam`, and its terminal is `64Theta/H^2`.
   334	
   335	The present chart imposes `CSTP-1` and only localizes `mu` by
   336	`mu*mu_inv-1` (`k4ray-pinned-chart-gpt55-20260903.md:102-114`).  Therefore the
   337	Theta constants above assume `CST=1` while `mu` remains a variable.  Do not also
   338	set `mu=1`: the displayed grading has only one scaling parameter, with
   339	`w(mu)=K+2` from `pinned_chart.py:148-154`, while `CST` has its own nonzero
   340	weight.  An alternative `mu=1` slice is safe over the algebraic closure only if
   341	`CST` is kept nonzero via a separate Rabinowitsch localizer, in which case every
   342	Theta above must be multiplied by `CST`.
   343	
   344	The main ideals are inhomogeneous localizations, so a modular unit remains only
   345	an F_p statement until an exact-Q computation confirms it; the charged report
   346	states this at `k4ray-pinned-chart-gpt55-20260903.md:292-310`.  A POSDIM result
   347	for the quotient screener is not a point of the full Jacobian chart.  Even a
   348	full-chart point is not a counterexample until its reconstructed Jacobian is
   349	checked exactly, per `FALLACY-v2.md:14-21,29-30`.
   350	
   351	Finally, the tower shape itself has a charged residual proof obligation:
   352	`a_2=0,a_1=3beta,a_0=(3/2)alpha` is described as normalized but its full
   353	band-by-band induction is not proved at
   354	`k4ray-unsplit-lemma-opus5-20260903.md:125-146`, and the open is restated at
   355	`k4ray-unsplit-lemma-opus5-20260903.md:467-475`.  A conditional chart kill is
   356	not an unconditional census promotion unless that obligation is discharged or
   357	the campaign already has an independent accepted source for the tower form.
   165	### 4.2 MASTER
   166	
   167	> **MASTER THEOREM (uniform in `K ≥ 7`).** For a ray-`R_4` tower pair with
   168	> `J(f,g) = c x⁴`, `c ≠ 0`, there is a **unique** `λ ∈ k` with
   169	> ```
   170	>                 deg ( g^2 - f^3 - lambda f )  =  K + 6 .
   171	> ```
   172	> Consequently `deg(g²−f³) ≤ 2K` and `deg_y(g²−f³) ≤ 2K`.
   173	> For `4 ≤ K ≤ 6` one has `λ = 0` and `deg(g²−f³) = K+6` exactly.
   174	
   175	*Proof.* `E ≠ 0` (else `g² = f³` and `J = 0`). By the band lemma, either
   176	`D = K+6` (take `λ = 0`), or `K ∣ D`, `E_D = λH^{D/K}`, `D > K+6`. In the second
   177	case `deg_y E_D = D`, because `H` is monic in `y` of `y`-degree `K`, so
   178	`deg_y H^{m} = mK`; and `deg_y E = max_D deg_y E_D` because distinct bands share
   179	no monomial. LEMMA YDEG then forces `D ≤ 3K−1`. The multiples of `K` in
   180	`(K+6, 3K−1]` are exactly `{2K}` for `K ≥ 7` and **none** for `K ≤ 6`
   181	(`MARK C2` table, `struct_checks.out`, `K = 4…15`). So `D = 2K` and
   182	`E_{2K} = λH² = λ·lf(f)`. Put `E' := E − λf ≠ 0` (else `J(f,E) = 0`). Then
   183	`J(f,E') = 2cx⁴g` still, `deg E' < 2K`, `deg_y E' ≤ 3K−1`, and the same
   184	dichotomy applies to `E'`: `deg E' = K+6`, or `K ∣ deg E'` with
   185	`K+6 < deg E' < 2K` — and there is no multiple of `K` in `(K+6, 2K)` for
   186	`K ≥ 7`. Uniqueness of `λ` is immediate from `deg f = 2K > K+6`. ∎
   187	
   188	### 4.3 The terminal form `Θ` is explicit
   189	
   190	Comparing leading forms in `J(f, E−λf) = 2c x⁴ g` gives, with
   191	`Θ := (E−λf)_{K+6}`,
   192	
   193	```text
   194	                    J( H , Theta )  =  c x^4 H^2 .
   195	```
   196	
   197	Solved exactly over **Q** as a linear system in the `K+7` coefficients of `Θ`,
   198	for `K = 7…14`: `MARK_THETA_UNIQUE 0` (zero free parameters),
   199	`MARK_THETA_RESID 0`, `MARK_THETA_DIV 0` in all eight (`theta_solve.out`). The
   200	solution is
   201	
   202	```text
   203	   Theta = y^K (y-x)^2 * Theta_1 ,     Theta_1 = sum_{i=0..4} e_i x^(4-i) y^i ,
   204	   e_0 = c/(5K-6) ,    e_i = (5-i) K e_{i-1} / ( (5-i) K - 6 )   for i = 1..4 .
   205	```
   206	
   207	(The denominators `(5−i)K−6` are nonzero exactly when `K ∤ 6`; `K = 6` is the
   208	excluded case.) Printed at `K = 7, 8, 9`:
   209	
   210	```text
   211	K=7  Theta_1 ∝ 110 x^4 + 140 x^3 y + 196 x^2 y^2 + 343 x y^3 + 2401 y^4
   212	K=8  Theta_1 ∝ 195 x^4 + 240 x^3 y + 320 x^2 y^2 + 512 x y^3 + 2048 y^4
   213	K=9  Theta_1 ∝  35 x^4 +  42 x^3 y +  54 x^2 y^2 +  81 x y^3 +  243 y^4
   214	```
   215	
   216	The valuation reading of `y^K(y−x)² ∣ Θ` is worth recording: `v_y(Θ) ≥ K` and
   217	`v_{y−x}(Θ) ≥ 2` follow from the ODE `Kηθ' − (K+6)η'θ = cη²`
   218	(`η := H(1,y) = y^{K−1}(y−1)`) because the indicial roots
   219	`σ = (K+6)(K−1)/K` and `τ = (K+6)/K` are **non-integral** exactly when `K ∤ 6`.
   220	
   221	---
   222	
   223	## 5. What MASTER gives: the whole charged tower, one line each
   224	
   225	**Scope: `K ≥ 7` throughout this section**, where MASTER reads `deg E ≤ 2K`;
   226	`4 ≤ K ≤ 6`, where the threshold is `K+6` instead, is done in §8.4.
   227	Write `P := β_b`, `A := α_{2b−K}`, `R := ρ_{3b−2K}`, `d := deg ρ`. Degrees in
   228	E-CUBIC: `deg β³ = 3b`, `deg(ρh²) = d+2K`, `deg(βρ) = b+d`, `deg α² = 4b−2K`;
   229	and `b < 2K` makes `b+d < d+2K` and `4b−2K < 3b`.
   230	
   231	**LEVEL 2 (= charged TOP-BAND).** `[E]_{2b+2K} = −3·[ρ]_{2b}·H²`
   232	(`MARK_EBAND_TOP_* 0` and `MARK_A2_ALL 0`, four instances, `eband_top.out`;
   233	the other three E-CUBIC terms have degrees `3b`, `b+d ≤ 3b`, `4b−2K`, all
   234	`< 2b+2K`). Since `2b+2K > 2K`, MASTER kills the band, so `[ρ]_{2b} = 0`, i.e.
   235	`H ∣ P²`, i.e. `y^{⌈(K−1)/2⌉}(y−x) ∣ P`. **This is 17(vvvvv) §4.2.**
   236	
   237	**LEVEL 3 (= charged ρ-DEGREE).** If `d > 3b−2K` then `d+2K > 3b` and
   238	`[E]_{d+2K} = −3ρ_d H² ≠ 0` with `d+2K > 2K` — killed by MASTER. Hence
   239	`deg ρ ≤ 3b−2K`. **This is 17(yyyyy) §3.2, with no `J`-band bookkeeping at all.**
   240	
   241	**LEVEL 4 (NEW).** Now `deg(ρh²) ≤ 3b` and `[E]_{3b} = P³ − 3RH²`. Feeding
   242	LEVEL 3 into the charged one-liner reconstructed in §2 gives `3b ≥ 2K+1 > 2K`
   243	(LEVEL 4 is therefore *downstream* of that bound, not an independent proof of
   244	it), and MASTER then kills the band:
   245	
   246	> **LEVEL-4 LEMMA (uniform in `K ≥ 7`).**
   247	> ```
   248	>            H^2  |  beta_b^3       and       rho_{3b-2K}  =  beta_b^3 / (3 H^2) ,
   249	> ```
   250	> and `deg ρ = 3b−2K` **exactly** (if `R` were `0`, `P³ = 0`).
   251	
   252	*Machine.* The closed form is verified directly: for `K = 7, 8, 9, 10, 12` and
   253	four shape families each, `A·J(H,P) = H·J(H,R)` holds with `A = P²/H`,
   254	`R = P³/(3H²)`, together with `deg_y P ≤ K−1`, `deg_y A ≤ K−2`,
   255	`deg_y R ≤ K−1`, `deg R = 3b−2K`: `MARK_E_SOLVES 0` in **20 of 20**,
   256	`MARK_E_ALL 0` (`level4_closed.out`). The competing homogeneous solution
   257	`R + (2/3)λH^{(3b−2K)/K}` of the same first-order equation is excluded by
   258	LEMMA INJ plus `deg_y R ≤ K−1`: it needs `K ∣ 3b` **and** `3b−2K ≥ K`, i.e.
   259	`b ≥ K`, **and** `b ≤ K−1` — empty for every `K` (`MARK E2`, `K = 7,8,9,12`).
   260	
   261	**LEVEL 4′ (NEW, the `y`-degree side).** MASTER also gives `deg_y E ≤ 2K`. In
   262	E-CUBIC the two `y`-leading terms are `−3ρh²` (`deg_y = deg_yρ + 2K`) and `β³`
   263	(`deg_y = 3 deg_yβ`), the other two being strictly smaller. Therefore:
   264	
   265	* if `deg_y ρ = 0` then `R = c_R x^{3b−2K}` and LEVEL 4 reads
   266	  `P³ = 3c_R x^{3b−2K} y^{2K−2}(y−x)²`, whose `(y−x)`-multiplicity is `2 ≢ 0 mod 3`
   267	  — **not a cube**. Contradiction. So `ρ ∉ k[x]`.
   268	* hence `deg_yρ ≥ 1`; and if `deg_yρ + 2K > 3 deg_yβ` the `y`-band
   269	  `[y^{deg_yρ+2K}]E = −3·(y‑lead of ρ) ≠ 0` would give
   270	  `deg_y E = deg_yρ+2K > 2K`, contradicting MASTER. So `deg_yρ + 2K ≤ 3 deg_yβ`,
   360	   8  :    6     15      10        20 :   14     39      26
   361	   9  :    7     17      11        50 :   34     99      66
   362	```
   363	
   364	`width / K → 4/3`. **The residual stratum is not bounded; it grows linearly in
   365	`K`.** This is the honest answer to (4).
   366	
   367	### 7.2 …but its bottom is *pinned*, and that is the wall row
   368	
   369	LEVEL 4 does not only bound `b`; it determines the shape of `β_b` at the bottom
   370	of the band. Writing `P = μ y^s (y−x)^t x^u Q̃` with `3s ≥ 2(K−1)`, `t ≥ 1`,
   371	`s+t+deg Q̃ = deg_y P ≤ min(b, K−1)`, the count of admissible shapes at
   372	`b = b_min` is **one** for every `K = 4…14` (`struct_checks.out` C4, column
   373	"pinned"):
   374	
   375	```text
   376	   K = 7,  b = 5  :  beta_5 = mu * y^4 (y-x)                 (1 scalar, was 6)
   377	   K = 8,  b = 6  :  beta_6 = mu * y^5 (y-x)                 (1 scalar, was 7)   <-- MEASURED wall row
   378	   K = 9,  b = 7  :  beta_7 = mu * y^6 (y-x)                 (1 scalar, was 8)   <-- MEASURED wall row
   379	```
   380	
   381	and then `ρ_{3b−2K} = μ³ y^{3s−2K+2}(y−x)/3` is forced too. The two rows that
   382	`SCUT_K7_B6`/`SCUT_K9_B7`/`MOD_K7_B6` could not finish at 55–80 parameters are
   383	exactly the rows where the top band of `β` is now a single scalar. That is a
   384	concrete, cheap cut for the next chart lane — it is *not* a kill, and I do not
   385	present it as one.
   386	
   387	Two consistency notes, both against the charged census:
   388	
   389	* `K = 9, b = 5` — the exceptional case `3b = K+6` that 17(yyyyy) §3.3 had to
   390	  kill by hand — is below `b_min = 7`, so LEVEL 4 excludes it outright.
   391	* `K = 7, b = 5` **is** admissible under LEVEL 4 (pinned to `μy⁴(y−x)`), yet the
   392	  charged machine killed it (`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, 9.8 s). So LEVEL 4 is strictly
   393	  weaker than the exact chart there: the ladder is genuinely incomplete, and I
   394	  say so rather than claiming coverage.
   395	
   396	---
   397	
   398	## 8. Controls
   399	
   400	### 8.1 Positive control — `K = 1`, target `x¹` (`PC_K1_B1_x1` of 17(yyyyy))
   401	
   402	`h = y−x`, `β = μx`, `α = 0`, `f = (y−x)²+2μx`, `g = (y−x)³+3μx(y−x)`,
   403	`J(f,g) = 6μ²x`. Then `E = g²−f³ = −μ²x²(8μx + 3(y−x)²)`, `deg E = 4 = K+k+2`
   404	with `k = 1` — the band lemma's terminal degree, **attained**; and
   405	`Θ = E₄ = −3μ²x²(y−x)²` satisfies `J(H,Θ) = 6μ²x·H²` exactly
   465	
   466	```text
   467	  Moh p.207-209  ->  ray R_4 data, Jacobian column X^4, deg_y B2 < deg h   [charged, primary]
   468	  17(vvvvv) §2.3 ->  deg_y beta <= K-1, lf(f)=H^2, lf(g)=H^3               [charged, PROVED]
   469	  17(vvvvv) §3.2 ->  beta in k => h | J => dead                            [charged, PROVED, deg beta = 0 only]
   470	  LEMMA BF + LEMMA INJ                                                     [re-proved, 196/196 machine]
   471	  E-CUBIC + JfE + LEMMA YDEG (deg_y E <= 3K-1, sharp)                      [PROVED HERE, 7/7 machine]
   472	  BAND LEMMA                                                              [PROVED HERE]
   473	     |
   474	     +-- MASTER: deg(g^2-f^3-lambda f) = K+6, deg E <= 2K                  [PROVED HERE, K >= 7]
   475	             |
   476	             +-- LEVEL 2  H | beta_b^2            = 17(vvvvv) §4.2 TOP-BAND      [re-proved, 1 line]
   477	             +-- LEVEL 3  deg rho <= 3b-2K        = 17(yyyyy) §3.2 rho-DEGREE    [re-proved, 1 line]
   478	             +-- 17(yyyyy) §3.3 one-liner (reconstructed §2) applied to LEVEL 3 => 3b >= 2K+1
   479	             +-- LEVEL 4  H^2 | beta_b^3, rho_{3b-2K} = beta_b^3/(3H^2)          [NEW; needs 3b > 2K]
   480	             |     `-- numerical shadow  3 deg beta >= 2K+1                      [reproduced, NOT independent
   481	             |                                                                    => SATURATION]
   482	             +-- LEVEL 4' rho not in k[x];  3 deg_y beta >= 2K+1;  deg_y rho <= K-3   [NEW]
