     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Minimal staged quotient-recurrence screen for the K=8,9 k=4-ray rows.
     3	
     4	This is a *necessary-subsystem* screen.  It uses one torus normalization only:
     5	the Jacobian coefficient is normalized to ``c=1`` through the explicit terminal
     6	form Theta, while the top beta coefficient ``mu`` remains a variable and is
     7	localized by ``mu*mu_inv-1``.  In particular, this file never sets both c and
     8	mu to 1.
     9	
    10	For ``q=beta^3/h^2`` in descending homogeneous bands, write
    11	
    12	    h_i = [h]_(K-i),  p_i = [beta]_(K-2-i),
    13	    S_n = sum_(a+b=n) h_a h_b,
    14	    T_n = sum_(a+b+c=n) p_a p_b p_c,
    15	    N_n = T_n - sum_(i=1..n) S_i q_(n-i).
    16	
    17	Then ``N_n=H^2 q_n``.  The K+6 MASTER theorem forces the positive quotient
    18	bands described below, zero intervening negative bands, and
    19	``N_(2K-12)=Theta``.  Closed exact parametrizations of n=1,2,3 eliminate the
    20	first lower h/beta bands without dividing by y or y-x.  Later h_n bands enter
    21	linearly through a constant Q matrix times the localized unit mu^3; exact RREF
    22	removes them and emits only compatibility equations.
    23	
    24	K=9 has two exhaustive UFD branches at n=3:
    25	
    26	    A: y divides v;
    27	    B: y divides (y-x)*v^2 - 12*mu*p_2.
    28	
    29	Both branches must be exact-Q unit ideals to kill K=9.  A modular unit is
    30	reported only as F_p evidence and is never promoted.  Durable band files are
    31	emitted with ``staged_band_emitter`` and every decision call goes through
    32	``guided_gb`` with a per-call timeout and a <=5-core budget.
    33	"""
