   165	### 4.2 MASTER
   166	
   167	> **MASTER THEOREM (uniform in `K ≥ 7`).** For a ray-`R_4` tower pair with
   168	> `J(f,g) = c x⁴`, `c ≠ 0`, there is a **unique** `λ ∈ k` with
   169	> ```
   170	>                 deg ( g^2 - f^3 - lambda f )  =  K + 6 .
   171	> ```
   172	> Consequently `deg(g²−f³) ≤ 2K` and `deg_y(g²−f³) ≤ 2K`.
   173	> For `4 ≤ K ≤ 6` one has `λ = 0` and `deg(g²−f³) = K+6` exactly.
   174	
   175	*Proof.* `E ≠ 0` (else `g² = f³` and `J = 0`). By the band lemma, either
   176	`D = K+6` (take `λ = 0`), or `K ∣ D`, `E_D = λH^{D/K}`, `D > K+6`. In the second
   177	case `deg_y E_D = D`, because `H` is monic in `y` of `y`-degree `K`, so
   178	`deg_y H^{m} = mK`; and `deg_y E = max_D deg_y E_D` because distinct bands share
   179	no monomial. LEMMA YDEG then forces `D ≤ 3K−1`. The multiples of `K` in
   180	`(K+6, 3K−1]` are exactly `{2K}` for `K ≥ 7` and **none** for `K ≤ 6`
   181	(`MARK C2` table, `struct_checks.out`, `K = 4…15`). So `D = 2K` and
   182	`E_{2K} = λH² = λ·lf(f)`. Put `E' := E − λf ≠ 0` (else `J(f,E) = 0`). Then
   183	`J(f,E') = 2cx⁴g` still, `deg E' < 2K`, `deg_y E' ≤ 3K−1`, and the same
   184	dichotomy applies to `E'`: `deg E' = K+6`, or `K ∣ deg E'` with
   185	`K+6 < deg E' < 2K` — and there is no multiple of `K` in `(K+6, 2K)` for
   186	`K ≥ 7`. Uniqueness of `λ` is immediate from `deg f = 2K > K+6`. ∎
   187	
   188	### 4.3 The terminal form `Θ` is explicit
   189	
   190	Comparing leading forms in `J(f, E−λf) = 2c x⁴ g` gives, with
   191	`Θ := (E−λf)_{K+6}`,
   192	
   193	```text
   194	                    J( H , Theta )  =  c x^4 H^2 .
   195	```
   196	
   197	Solved exactly over **Q** as a linear system in the `K+7` coefficients of `Θ`,
   198	for `K = 7…14`: `MARK_THETA_UNIQUE 0` (zero free parameters),
   199	`MARK_THETA_RESID 0`, `MARK_THETA_DIV 0` in all eight (`theta_solve.out`). The
   200	solution is
   201	
   202	```text
   203	   Theta = y^K (y-x)^2 * Theta_1 ,     Theta_1 = sum_{i=0..4} e_i x^(4-i) y^i ,
   204	   e_0 = c/(5K-6) ,    e_i = (5-i) K e_{i-1} / ( (5-i) K - 6 )   for i = 1..4 .
   205	```
   206	
   207	(The denominators `(5−i)K−6` are nonzero exactly when `K ∤ 6`; `K = 6` is the
   208	excluded case.) Printed at `K = 7, 8, 9`:
   209	
   210	```text
   211	K=7  Theta_1 ∝ 110 x^4 + 140 x^3 y + 196 x^2 y^2 + 343 x y^3 + 2401 y^4
   212	K=8  Theta_1 ∝ 195 x^4 + 240 x^3 y + 320 x^2 y^2 + 512 x y^3 + 2048 y^4
   213	K=9  Theta_1 ∝  35 x^4 +  42 x^3 y +  54 x^2 y^2 +  81 x y^3 +  243 y^4
   214	```
   215	
   216	The valuation reading of `y^K(y−x)² ∣ Θ` is worth recording: `v_y(Θ) ≥ K` and
   217	`v_{y−x}(Θ) ≥ 2` follow from the ODE `Kηθ' − (K+6)η'θ = cη²`
   218	(`η := H(1,y) = y^{K−1}(y−1)`) because the indicial roots
   219	`σ = (K+6)(K−1)/K` and `τ = (K+6)/K` are **non-integral** exactly when `K ∤ 6`.
   220	
   221	---
   222	
   223	## 5. What MASTER gives: the whole charged tower, one line each
   224	
   225	**Scope: `K ≥ 7` throughout this section**, where MASTER reads `deg E ≤ 2K`;
   226	`4 ≤ K ≤ 6`, where the threshold is `K+6` instead, is done in §8.4.
   227	Write `P := β_b`, `A := α_{2b−K}`, `R := ρ_{3b−2K}`, `d := deg ρ`. Degrees in
   228	E-CUBIC: `deg β³ = 3b`, `deg(ρh²) = d+2K`, `deg(βρ) = b+d`, `deg α² = 4b−2K`;
   229	and `b < 2K` makes `b+d < d+2K` and `4b−2K < 3b`.
   230	
   231	**LEVEL 2 (= charged TOP-BAND).** `[E]_{2b+2K} = −3·[ρ]_{2b}·H²`
   232	(`MARK_EBAND_TOP_* 0` and `MARK_A2_ALL 0`, four instances, `eband_top.out`;
   233	the other three E-CUBIC terms have degrees `3b`, `b+d ≤ 3b`, `4b−2K`, all
   234	`< 2b+2K`). Since `2b+2K > 2K`, MASTER kills the band, so `[ρ]_{2b} = 0`, i.e.
   235	`H ∣ P²`, i.e. `y^{⌈(K−1)/2⌉}(y−x) ∣ P`. **This is 17(vvvvv) §4.2.**
   236	
   237	**LEVEL 3 (= charged ρ-DEGREE).** If `d > 3b−2K` then `d+2K > 3b` and
   238	`[E]_{d+2K} = −3ρ_d H² ≠ 0` with `d+2K > 2K` — killed by MASTER. Hence
   239	`deg ρ ≤ 3b−2K`. **This is 17(yyyyy) §3.2, with no `J`-band bookkeeping at all.**
   240	
   241	**LEVEL 4 (NEW).** Now `deg(ρh²) ≤ 3b` and `[E]_{3b} = P³ − 3RH²`. Feeding
   242	LEVEL 3 into the charged one-liner reconstructed in §2 gives `3b ≥ 2K+1 > 2K`
   243	(LEVEL 4 is therefore *downstream* of that bound, not an independent proof of
   244	it), and MASTER then kills the band:
   245	
   246	> **LEVEL-4 LEMMA (uniform in `K ≥ 7`).**
   247	> ```
   248	>            H^2  |  beta_b^3       and       rho_{3b-2K}  =  beta_b^3 / (3 H^2) ,
   249	> ```
   250	> and `deg ρ = 3b−2K` **exactly** (if `R` were `0`, `P³ = 0`).
   251	
   252	*Machine.* The closed form is verified directly: for `K = 7, 8, 9, 10, 12` and
   253	four shape families each, `A·J(H,P) = H·J(H,R)` holds with `A = P²/H`,
   254	`R = P³/(3H²)`, together with `deg_y P ≤ K−1`, `deg_y A ≤ K−2`,
   255	`deg_y R ≤ K−1`, `deg R = 3b−2K`: `MARK_E_SOLVES 0` in **20 of 20**,
   256	`MARK_E_ALL 0` (`level4_closed.out`). The competing homogeneous solution
   257	`R + (2/3)λH^{(3b−2K)/K}` of the same first-order equation is excluded by
   258	LEMMA INJ plus `deg_y R ≤ K−1`: it needs `K ∣ 3b` **and** `3b−2K ≥ K`, i.e.
   259	`b ≥ K`, **and** `b ≤ K−1` — empty for every `K` (`MARK E2`, `K = 7,8,9,12`).
   260	
   261	**LEVEL 4′ (NEW, the `y`-degree side).** MASTER also gives `deg_y E ≤ 2K`. In
   262	E-CUBIC the two `y`-leading terms are `−3ρh²` (`deg_y = deg_yρ + 2K`) and `β³`
   263	(`deg_y = 3 deg_yβ`), the other two being strictly smaller. Therefore:
   264	
   265	* if `deg_y ρ = 0` then `R = c_R x^{3b−2K}` and LEVEL 4 reads
   266	  `P³ = 3c_R x^{3b−2K} y^{2K−2}(y−x)²`, whose `(y−x)`-multiplicity is `2 ≢ 0 mod 3`
   267	  — **not a cube**. Contradiction. So `ρ ∉ k[x]`.
   268	* hence `deg_yρ ≥ 1`; and if `deg_yρ + 2K > 3 deg_yβ` the `y`-band
   269	  `[y^{deg_yρ+2K}]E = −3·(y‑lead of ρ) ≠ 0` would give
   270	  `deg_y E = deg_yρ+2K > 2K`, contradicting MASTER. So `deg_yρ + 2K ≤ 3 deg_yβ`,
   271	  hence
   272	  ```
   273	                3 * deg_y(beta)  >=  2K + 1 ,      1 <= deg_y(rho) <= 3 deg_y(beta) - 2K <= K-3 .
   274	  ```
   275	
   115	Derivation (not assumption): with `β² = αh + ρ`, `deg_y ρ < K`,
   116	
   117	```
   118	g² − f³ = (2ε − 3α)h³ − 3ρh² + 9αβh + (9/4)α² − 8β³        for  g = h³ + 3βh + ε,
   119	```
   120	
   121	so `ε = (3/2)α` is precisely the choice that annihilates the `h³` band —
   122	i.e. `g` is `f^{3/2}` truncated. Verified exactly:
   123	`box/k4ray-20260903/identity_check.out` `MARK_ID3_GSQ 0`.
   124	
   125	### 2.3 What is proved about the shape, and what is not
   126	
   127	* **`lf(f) = H²`, `lf(g) = H³`.** For `K ≥ 2` the top Jacobian band
   128	  `J(lf f, lf g)` sits in degree `5K−2 > 4` and must vanish; for binary forms
   129	  `J(F,G) = 0` with `deg F = 2K`, `deg G = 3K` forces `F³ = λG²`, hence
   130	  `F = H²`, `G = H³` for a common form `H` of degree `K`. Consequently
   131	  `deg B ≤ 2K−1`, `deg a₂ ≤ K−1`, `deg a₁ ≤ 2K−1`, `deg a₀ ≤ 3K−1`.
   132	* **`deg_y B < K` is PROVED**, being the defining property of the approximate
   133	  root. This discharges the prompt's step-(3) obligation *in the `y` direction*.
   134	* **`a₂ = 0`, `a₁ = 3β`, `a₀ = (3/2)α` is a normalisation with a residual
   135	  obligation.** Its top band is proved here: matching band `3K−1` gives
   136	  `g_{3K−1} = (3/2)H·f_{2K−1}`, and since the three `h`-adic pieces
   137	  `a₂H², Ha₁, a₀` occupy the *disjoint* `y`-degree ranges `[2K, 3K−1]`,
   138	  `[K, 2K−1]`, `[0, K−1]`, the band separates into
   139	  `(a₂)_{K−1} = 0`, `(a₀)_{3K−1} = 0`, `(a₁)_{2K−1} = (3/2)B_{2K−1}`.
   140	  The same `y`-degree separation is available at every band, so the induction is
   141	  routine; I did not write it out band by band and do **not** claim it as proved.
   142	  Everything in §3 is stated in the *general* shape (no tower) precisely so that
   143	  the composite arm does not depend on it.
   144	* **`deg β ≤ K−1` (total degree) is NOT proved.** Only `deg β ≤ 2K−1` is. This
   145	  is the single scoping restriction on §5 and is raised as
   146	  `OPEN[K4RAY-BETA-DEG]`.
   147	
   148	---
   149	
