+## FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+- No flag, place, series, exit-set, pole, or M-descent assertion is made.
+- No new exit-price assertion is made, so no `charge_basis` declaration is
+  applicable.
+- The terminal degree `K+6` is used as the attained equality proved by MASTER,
+  not as an unattained floor.
+- No `sat()` operation is used. The explicit ideal component is the `mu!=0`
+  chart represented by `mu*mu_inv-1`; the solver ring and generator order are
+  serialized.
+- Monic long division in `y` or exact total-band identities construct
+  `alpha,rho`; no raw remainder degree is guessed and no vanished parameter
+  leader is divided out.
+- `x,y` live only in the coefficient-extraction polynomial ring. The map to the
+  parameter ring is by the explicitly serialized coefficient list, and every
+  emitted expression is checked to use only declared solver variables.
+- All prime numbers label coefficient fields; no prime notation denotes a
+  derivative in this report.
+- Modular units remain F_p-only. Only a clean exact-Q run can produce
+  `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`.
+- A positive-dimensional result on a necessary subsystem would not be a chart
+  point. A full-chart point would still require reconstruction of
+  `(f,g)=(h^2+2beta,h^3+3beta*h+(3/2)alpha)` and an exact computation of
+  `J=f_xg_y-f_yg_x`. No such inference is needed for the K=8 unit ideal.
