+
+| field | wall in standard-basis call | unit | basis size | dim | normal forms |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| F_32003 | 0.114422 s | yes | 1 | -1 | all 61 rows reduce to zero |
+| F_32009 | 0.114102 s | yes | 1 | -1 | all zero |
+| F_32027 | 0.114111 s | yes | 1 | -1 | all zero |
+
+Those three rows are only `UNIT_IN_EVERY_REQUESTED_FIBRE__FP_ONLY`. The
+separate exact run over `Q` then returned in 0.115332 seconds:
+
+```text
+returncode=0
+timed_out=false
+missing_markers=[]
+basis_size=1
+unit=true
+dimension=-1
+nf_all_zero=true
+verdict=UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0
+```
+
+The solver summary SHA-256 is
+`574c8b915fb43f9b86cfd22a9a9eb873a2c1f0bea4e24f230f5b26ebcd32fa31`.
+No CRT/properness inference enters the verdict; the exact rational reduction
+is the certificate.
+
+Therefore the K=8 nonconstant pinned arm is **DEAD**. By the charged promotion
+chain at `k4ray-pinned-chart-gpt55-20260903.md:332-343`, the D=108 no-split row
+is dead and **D=108 is CLOSED at skeleton level**.
+
+## K=9 decision
+
+For K=9, `r=3`, `phi=y*v`, and `v` is quadratic. The remaining polynomiality
+condition is
+
+```text
+y | v*(L*v^2-12*mu*p_2).
+```
+
+Because `(y)` is prime, its zero set is covered exactly by two closed charts:
+
+```text
+A: v=y*w;
+B: L*v^2-12*mu*p_2=y*zeta.
+```
+
+Their intersection is retained in both, and neither `v` nor the second factor
+is inverted. Writing
+
+```text
+omega=w*(L*y^2*w^2-12*mu*p_2)  on A,
+omega=v*zeta                    on B,
+```
+
+the third band becomes
+
+```text
+h_3=(omega+36*chi*v*y^3+24*mu^2*p_3*y^2
+     -18*v^2*tau-8*kappa*y^6)/(16*mu^3).
+```
+
+The remaining quotient recurrence is `N_4=0`, `N_5=0`,
+`N_6=Theta_9`. Exact constant-matrix RREF eliminates all coefficients of
+`h_4,h_5,h_6` in sequence. In both charts the pivot ranks are `6,5,4`, so 15
+variables disappear. Chart A leaves `6,8,12` compatibility rows and chart B
+leaves `6,9,12`; both reduced rings contain 36 variables including `mu_inv`.
+Independent static checks confirm the split identities, all RREF ranks, the
+absence of eliminated variables from reconstruction and solver rings, and
+integral emitted rows after denominator clearing.
+
+The raw 51-variable post-PIN12 chart still timed out at the first 180-second
+modular standard basis. That attempt is only a diagnostic and carries no
+verdict. The next subsection records the sparse alpha/rho bands and exact
+decisions for both exhaustive charts.
+
+### Sparse alpha/rho continuation
+
+PENDING.
+
+### Branch verdicts
+
+PENDING.
+
+## Controls
+
+All controls were replayed from the frozen inputs with Singular 4.3.2, one
+thread in every threaded library, and per-call bounds. The aggregate schema is
+`jc2.k4ray.controls-replay/v1`; status is `PASS`; total wall time is 9.194617
+seconds.
+
+| control | exact-Q result | wall | interpretation |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| charged K=7 pinned light | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, basis 1, dim -1, NF clean | 7.774979 s | reproduces the reported approximately 8-second kill |
+| charged K=4, b=3 | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, 61 rows | 0.015799 s | charged low-K empty calibration |
+| charged K=5, b=4 | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, 137 rows | 0.114120 s | charged low-K empty calibration |
+| tame `h=y-x`, `beta=mu*x` | nonunit, dim 0, vector-space length 2 | 0.007878 s | a nonempty tame chart survives; exact `J=6*x*mu^2` varies |
+| Hilbert-hint main run | accepted, dim 0, length 3640 | 1.015288 s | prediction and computed length agree |
+| perturbed hint | rejected despite computed length 3640 | same call | target mismatch is detected |
+
+For every unit control, `reduce(I,G)=0` and all required output markers are
+present. The tame control guards against a driver which labels every ideal
+unit; the perturbation guards against accepting a basis merely because a
+computed length exists. The controls artifact manifest contains 47 files and
+passes `sha256sum -c`.
+
+K=4 and K=5 are calibration rows, not census promotions. No conclusion about
+K=8 or K=9 is inferred from them.
+
+## K-uniform extension
+
+The reduction has exposed a uniform object, but not yet a uniform kill. For
+`b=K-2`, `r=K-6`, the quotient recurrence `REC_n` and the PIN12 formulas are
+closed in K; the terminal target is always
+
+```text
+Theta_K = y^K*(y-x)^2*sum_(i=0..4) e_i*x^(4-i)*y^i,
+e_0=1/(5K-6),
+e_i=((5-i)K/((5-i)K-6))*e_(i-1).
+```
+
+At K=9 the first genuinely new event is the exact two-factor split above.
+K=10 and K=11 are attempted only if both K=9 reduced branches become cheap:
+their terminal recurrence needs more zero bands and the split geometry is not
+automatically the K=9 two-chart geometry. A timeout is not extrapolated into a
+verdict. The target remains the closed-form killing combination requested for
+row `17(vvvvv)`, not a list of modular observations.
+
+## Skeleton promotions and verdicts
+
+PENDING K=9.
+
+## FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+- No flag, place, series, exit-set, pole, or M-descent assertion is made.
+- No new exit-price assertion is made, so no `charge_basis` declaration is
+  applicable.
+- The terminal degree `K+6` is used as the attained equality proved by MASTER,
+  not as an unattained floor.
+- No `sat()` operation is used. The explicit ideal component is the `mu!=0`
+  chart represented by `mu*mu_inv-1`; the solver ring and generator order are
+  serialized.
+- Monic long division in `y` or exact total-band identities construct
+  `alpha,rho`; no raw remainder degree is guessed and no vanished parameter
+  leader is divided out.
+- `x,y` live only in the coefficient-extraction polynomial ring. The map to the
+  parameter ring is by the explicitly serialized coefficient list, and every
+  emitted expression is checked to use only declared solver variables.
+- All prime numbers label coefficient fields; no prime notation denotes a
+  derivative in this report.
+- Modular units remain F_p-only. Only a clean exact-Q run can produce
+  `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`.
+- A positive-dimensional result on a necessary subsystem would not be a chart
+  point. A full-chart point would still require reconstruction of
+  `(f,g)=(h^2+2beta,h^3+3beta*h+(3/2)alpha)` and an exact computation of
+  `J=f_xg_y-f_yg_x`. No such inference is needed for the K=8 unit ideal.
+
