+## K-uniform extension
+
+The reduction has exposed a uniform object, but not yet a uniform kill. For
+`b=K-2`, `r=K-6`, the quotient recurrence `REC_n` and the PIN12 formulas are
+closed in K; the terminal target is always
+
+```text
+Theta_K = y^K*(y-x)^2*sum_(i=0..4) e_i*x^(4-i)*y^i,
+e_0=1/(5K-6),
+e_i=((5-i)K/((5-i)K-6))*e_(i-1).
+```
+
+At K=9 the first genuinely new event is the exact two-factor split above.
+K=10 and K=11 are attempted only if both K=9 reduced branches become cheap:
+their terminal recurrence needs more zero bands and the split geometry is not
+automatically the K=9 two-chart geometry. A timeout is not extrapolated into a
+verdict. The target remains the closed-form killing combination requested for
+row `17(vvvvv)`, not a list of modular observations.
