@@ -0,0 +1,635 @@
+# Exact-Q closure of the nonconstant k=4-ray rows K=8 and K=9
+
+Date: 2026-09-04  
+Lane: `k4ray-K89-sol56-20260903`  
+Status: complete; both rows decided by exact-Q unit certificates
+
+## Verdict at a glance
+
+This lane replaces the 58- and 74-variable top-pin computations by exact
+lower-band parametrizations before asking for a standard basis.
+
+| row | reduced necessary chart | characteristic-zero decision | consequence |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| K=8, b=6, D=108 no-split `(24,16;18;7;4)` | 36 ring variables; 61 band rows plus the `mu` localizer | **`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`** | row dead; D=108 closed at skeleton level |
+| K=9, b=7, `(99,66)` case (A), internal split A | 36 variables; 96 rows plus localizer | **`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`** | internal chart dead |
+| K=9, b=7, `(99,66)` case (A), internal split B | 36 variables; 98 rows plus localizer | **`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`** | internal chart dead; case (A) dead |
+
+None of these decisions is a modular lift. In every row three good finite-field
+fibres die, and a separate standard-basis computation over `Q` gives the
+one-element basis `[1]`, `dim=-1`, and `reduce(I,G)=0`. The modular computations
+are recorded only as screens because the charts contain the inhomogeneous
+equation `mu*mu_inv-1`.
+
+## Scope and decision standard
+
+This report records the reduced-chart construction, staged and modular screens,
+mandatory exact-rational decisions, controls, and any resulting skeleton
+promotions for the two outstanding nonconstant arms:
+
+- K=8, D=108 no-split `(24,16; 18; 7; 4)`, b=6;
+- K=9, case (A) of `(99,66)`, `(27,18; 21; 8; 4)`, b=7.
+
+Only an exact-Q unit certificate closes a row as dead.  Positive-dimensional
+output is followed by point extraction and an exact Jacobian test.  Finite-field
+unit output is used only as a screen and is never promoted directly.
+
+## Frozen-input verification
+
+The charged files were read only from `/tmp/jc2-lane.HDMqeS/inputs`. The
+manifest was generated from the lane receipt, not transcribed from the prompt:
+
+```bash
+receipt=xmodel/k4ray-K89-sol56-20260903.run.v2
+manifest=/tmp/k4ray-K89-sol56-20260903.sha256
+awk -F= '
+  $1 == "lane_inputs_dir" { input_dir=$2 }
+  $1 ~ /^charged_input_[[:digit:]]+_basename$/ {
+    split($1, part, "_"); basename[part[3]]=$2
+  }
+  $1 ~ /^charged_input_[[:digit:]]+_sha256$/ {
+    split($1, part, "_");
+    print $2 "  " input_dir "/" basename[part[3]]
+  }
+' "$receipt" > "$manifest"
+sha256sum -c "$manifest"
+```
+
+All nine entries returned `OK`. The same generated manifest was checked a
+second time, also with nine `OK` results. In receipt order the verified
+digests are:
+
+```text
+db150d8b078b9626348dd75dc21f966b20671e070e2c2349c1224bf2a46f130f  k4ray-pinned-chart-gpt55-20260903.md
+2befb3cac8e51305e65ab0e48de485a7098ba104a3620d8b174927791a896a2a  k4ray-degree-tower-opus5-20260903.md
+8cda501a0ea448fe4bbf0703930a2aa5d2ee8f7bfcbc70b34ea133bb650926bd  k4ray-unsplit-lemma-opus5-20260903.md
+3256f9599f92f5f7e2129d4164237296f2adbce8bcda8fd61f56474ecdd55e6c  sys-guided-gb-gpt55-20260903.md
+501f3b1fed8ad0d26c7535a3c79d6ca74c448a4555f94570a4835d9f740781f3  guided_gb.py
+7c2f88430158fc01b2aa4e1bc2af1902f92168d10cd48ee5095506beb149dce8  staged_band_emitter.py
+d20bf0841a1ba2b229d423bb948e6c4474a4f5a83f55148071cae39cb6c506c2  moh_skeleton_full.py
+e47fd16cfcc91bc7bfdac4ba1b5f46152db8235e6609dca6e29a5966549c38f5  FALLACY-v2.md
+eed2cdf5cc5b85e3358013416bca7f6f6bd272138533ff0c065a86afb4c47e43  pinned_chart.py
+```
+
+## Algebraic conventions and maps
+
+Put `L=y-x`, `b=K-2`, and
+
+```text
+H = y^(K-1)L,
+beta_b = P = mu*y^(K-3)L,
+f = h^2 + 2 beta,
+g = h^3 + 3 beta*h + (3/2) alpha,
+beta^2 = alpha*h + rho.
+```
+
+These are beta coordinates. The frozen driver instead writes
+`B=2 beta`, `Al=4 alpha`, `Rh=4 rho`; no factor from that scaled convention is
+silently imported here. The identity used is
+
+```text
+E := g^2-f^3
+   = beta^3 - 3*rho*h^2 - 9*beta*rho + (9/4)*alpha^2.
+```
+
+The charged MASTER theorem gives a unique scalar `lambda` for `K>=7` with
+
+```text
+deg(E-lambda*f)=K+6,       deg(E)<=2K,
+```
+
+and its attained terminal band `Theta=[E-lambda*f]_(K+6)` is the unique binary
+form satisfying
+
+```text
+J(H,Theta)=c*x^4*H^2.
+```
+
+References are
+`k4ray-degree-tower-opus5-20260903.md:49-68,115-137,141-219`.
+LEVEL 4 supplies the necessary equality
+
+```text
+H^2 | beta_b^3,
+rho_(3b-2K) = beta_b^3/(3H^2),
+deg rho = 3b-2K,
+```
+
+at that source's lines 223-259. Thus for the two rows here
+`3b-2K=K-6`, and the top pin is exactly the displayed `P`.
+
+The coefficient field of every promoted calculation is `Q`. The solver
+variables are chart parameters only; `x,y` are coefficient-extraction
+bookkeeping variables and do not enter the standard-basis ring. A typical
+solver ring is
+
+```text
+SS = Q,(parameters,mu,remaining-h-coefficients,mu_inv),wp(weights)
+```
+
+with positive tower weights, variables ordered by decreasing weight, and
+`mu_inv` last. The sole localization is
+
+```text
+mu*mu_inv-1.
+```
+
+Neither `y` nor `y-x` is inverted. The Jacobian scalar is normalized once by
+choosing `c=CST=1`; `mu` remains a variable. This is the same inhomogeneous
+localization posture as the charged pinned chart
+(`k4ray-pinned-chart-gpt55-20260903.md:102-114`).
+
+The census promotion is consequently a statement about the charged
+nonconstant pinned/tower arm. The separate charged source labels the full
+derivation of the normalized tower and the total-degree beta bound as residual
+obligations (`k4ray-unsplit-lemma-opus5-20260903.md:125-146,467-475`). This
+lane does not manufacture those missing implications; it decides the chart
+which the task places downstream of them.
+
+## Reduction beyond the top-band pin
+
+### Formal quotient recurrence
+
+Write total-degree bands
+
+```text
+h_i = [h]_(K-i),        h_0=H,
+p_i = [beta]_(b-i),     p_0=P,
+S_n = sum_(a+b=n) h_a*h_b,
+T_n = sum_(a+b+c=n) p_a*p_b*p_c.
+```
+
+For the formal quotient `q=beta^3/h^2`, define its bands without ever dividing
+by `H`:
+
+```text
+N_n = T_n - sum_(i=1..n) S_i*q_(n-i),
+N_n = H^2*q_n.                                      (REC_n)
+```
+
+Let `r=K-6`. Degree comparison in the exact cubic identity shows that all
+terms except `beta^3-(3rho+lambda)h^2` are below the terminal degree `K+6`.
+The necessary bands are therefore
+
+```text
+q_i = 3*rho_(r-i)          for 0 <= i < r,
+q_r = 3*rho_0 + lambda     (one free scalar),
+q_i = 0                    for r < i < 2r,
+N_(2r) = +Theta.
+```
+
+The terminal sign is positive and there is no scale factor when `p_i` are beta
+bands. The construction uses polynomial coefficient identities throughout;
+there is no `sat()` call and no division by an `x,y` form.
+
+### The first two lower bands: PIN12
+
+Solving `REC_1` and `REC_2` pointwise on `mu!=0` gives
+
+```text
+deg(tau)=K-7,      deg(phi)=K-6,      deg(chi)=K-8,
+
+p_1 = y^2*(3*y^2*tau-L*phi),
+h_1 = (3/mu)*y^6*tau - (3/(2mu))*y^4*L*phi,
+
+h_2 = (3/(2mu^2)) *
+      (mu*y^2*p_2 + (1/4)*y^(9-K)*L*phi^2 - y^6*chi),
+
+q_1=3*mu^2*tau,       q_2=3*mu*chi,
+[y^(K-6)]phi = 2*[y^(K-7)]tau.                     (PIN12)
+```
+
+The divisibility step is `y^(K-5)|psi^2`, which forces `y^2|psi` for K=8,9;
+it covers `psi=0` and introduces no open chart. In the emitted polynomial
+formulae every `1/mu` is replaced by `mu_inv`, modulo the retained localizer.
+PIN12 removes 15 geometric coefficients before later recurrence bands.
+
+The actual remainder bands, not merely the formal quotient bands, are then
+matched:
+
+```text
+K=8: rho_2=(1/3)*mu^3*y*L, rho_1=mu^2*tau, deg(rho)<=2;
