+`6550cfa5b3e1f1ada1a30446734cc386cdaa1bcfe7c139b60ddbfed9f902b08f`.
+The combined exhaustive-cover promotion summary has SHA-256
+`a7ec2b0af3d860f51a60d31257c0ae5e36eeefc064e259f0ab38bb3e033d72d5`.
+
+Therefore both exhaustive factors of `K9-SPLIT` are
+**`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`**. The K=9 nonconstant pinned/tower arm has no point; no
+reconstruction or Jacobian-constancy test is triggered. The outer `(99,66)`
+case (A) is **DEAD**.
+
+## Controls
+
+All controls were replayed from the frozen inputs with Singular 4.3.2, one
+thread in every threaded library, and per-call bounds. The aggregate schema is
+`jc2.k4ray.controls-replay/v1`; status is `PASS`; total wall time is 9.194617
+seconds.
+
+| control | exact-Q result | wall | interpretation |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| charged K=7 pinned light | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, basis 1, dim -1, NF clean | 7.774979 s | reproduces the reported approximately 8-second kill |
+| charged K=4, b=3 | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, 61 rows | 0.015799 s | charged low-K empty calibration |
+| charged K=5, b=4 | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, 137 rows | 0.114120 s | charged low-K empty calibration |
+| tame `h=y-x`, `beta=mu*x` | nonunit, dim 0, vector-space length 2 | 0.007878 s | a nonempty tame chart survives; exact `J=6*x*mu^2` varies |
+| Hilbert-hint main run | accepted, dim 0, length 3640 | 1.015288 s | prediction and computed length agree |
+| perturbed hint | rejected despite computed length 3640 | same call | target mismatch is detected |
+
+For every unit control, `reduce(I,G)=0` and all required output markers are
+present. The tame control guards against a driver which labels every ideal
+unit; the perturbation guards against accepting a basis merely because a
+computed length exists. The controls artifact manifest contains 47 files and
+passes `sha256sum -c`. The controls summary SHA-256 is
+`c26c07d5a2e14ab3c6defe6e8db63a66e3835a04c5e1e45c4a82ae9d79fef8c6`.
+
+K=4 and K=5 are calibration rows, not census promotions. No conclusion about
+K=8 or K=9 is inferred from them.
+
+## K-uniform extension
+
+The reduction has exposed a uniform recurrence, but not yet a uniform kill.
+For `b=K-2`, `r=K-6`, the quotient recurrence `REC_n` is closed in K. For
+`7<=K<=13` (in particular K=10,11), the other terms in `E-lambda*f` are below
+degree `K+6`, so the terminal target is
+
+```text
+Theta_K = y^K*(y-x)^2*sum_(i=0..4) e_i*x^(4-i)*y^i,
+e_0=1/(5K-6),
+e_i=((5-i)K/((5-i)K-6))*e_(i-1).
+```
+
+At K=10 the initial divisibility exponent changes. In general write
+`psi=y^s*phi`, `s=ceil((K-5)/2)`, so `s=3` for K=10,11. An exact symbolic-Q
+expansion of `REC_3`, independently checked twice, gives after `phi=y*v`
+
+```text
+K=10: y | p_2*v,
+K=11: y^2 | v*W,  W=(y-x)*v^2-18*v*tau-12*mu*p_2.
+```
+
+Thus K=10 has the two exhaustive closed charts `v=y*w` and `p_2=y*zeta`.
+K=11 has the three valuation charts
+
+```text
+ord_y(v)>=2;
+ord_y(v)>=1 and ord_y(W)>=1;
+ord_y(W)>=2.
+```
+
+Overlaps are retained; no factor is localized. The same audit recovers
+
+```text
+Theta_10 = y^10*(y-x)^2*(119*x^4+140*x^3*y+175*x^2*y^2
+                         +250*x*y^3+625*y^4)/5236,
+Theta_11 = y^11*(y-x)^2*(3420*x^4+3960*x^3*y+4840*x^2*y^2
+                         +6655*x*y^3+14641*y^4)/167580.
+```
+
+This is the bounded K-uniform push, not a K=10 or K=11 census verdict. K=10
+projects from 91 raw geometric coefficients to 75 after the new pin and 67
+after `REC_3`; full-rank elimination of `h_4,...,h_8` would leave a predicted
+44-variable ring including `mu_inv`, across five terminal bands. K=11 projects
+`111 -> 95 -> 86`, then to a predicted 55-variable ring across seven terminal
+bands and three valuation charts. Since the K=9 one-core formations already
+took 205.58 and 368.20 seconds for only three terminal bands, neither extension
+was a cheap reuse; no K=10/11 Groebner job was launched and no modular or
+characteristic-zero verdict is claimed. The next constructive target is a
+branch-aware constant-Q RREF for `N_4,...,N_(2r)`, followed by sparse
+alpha/remainder matching. The closed-form killing row `17(vvvvv)` remains the
+target.
+
+## Skeleton promotions and verdicts
+
+The two exact-Q chains are:
+
+```text
+K=8 reduced necessary ideal = (1)
+  => K=8 nonconstant pinned row DEAD
+  => D=108 no-split row DEAD
+  => D=108 CLOSED at skeleton level.
+
+K=9 internal split A reduced necessary ideal = (1)
+and K=9 internal split B reduced necessary ideal = (1)
+and {internal A, internal B} is an exhaustive cover
+  => K=9 nonconstant pinned row DEAD
+  => case (A) of (99,66) DEAD
+  => with banked configurations (B) and (C),
+     (99,66) SKELETON VERDICT COMPLETE for all three configurations modulo N1.
+```
+
+Final row verdicts:
+
+```text
+K=8, D=108 no-split (24,16;18;7;4), b=6:
+  UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0 — DEAD.
+
+K=9, (99,66) case (A) (27,18;21;8;4), b=7:
+  internal split A UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0;
+  internal split B UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0;
+  exhaustive union DEAD.
+
+D=108 skeleton closure:
+  CLOSED.
+
+(99,66) skeleton, all three configurations modulo N1:
+  COMPLETE.
+
+NOTIFY-WORTHY:
+  TRUE — this is the requested milestone.
+```
+
+These are emptiness promotions. There is no POSDIM survivor, Keller pair, or
+candidate counterexample to report.
+
+## FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+- No flag, place, series, exit-set, pole, or M-descent assertion is made.
+- No new exit-price assertion is made, so no `charge_basis` declaration is
+  applicable.
+- The terminal degree `K+6` is used as the attained equality proved by MASTER,
+  not as an unattained floor.
+- No `sat()` operation is used. The explicit ideal component is the `mu!=0`
+  chart represented by `mu*mu_inv-1`; the solver ring and generator order are
+  serialized.
+- Monic long division in `y` or exact total-band identities construct
+  `alpha,rho`; no raw remainder degree is guessed and no vanished parameter
+  leader is divided out.
+- `x,y` live only in the coefficient-extraction polynomial ring. The map to the
+  parameter ring is by the explicitly serialized coefficient list, and every
+  emitted expression is checked to use only declared solver variables.
+- All prime numbers label coefficient fields; no prime notation denotes a
+  derivative in this report.
+- Modular units remain F_p-only. Only a clean exact-Q run can produce
+  `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`.
+- A positive-dimensional result on a necessary subsystem would not be a chart
+  point. A full-chart point would still require reconstruction of
+  `(f,g)=(h^2+2beta,h^3+3beta*h+(3/2)alpha)` and an exact computation of
+  `J=f_xg_y-f_yg_x`. No such inference is needed because all three reduced
+  charts are exact-Q unit ideals.
+- The outer label “case (A) of `(99,66)`” is kept distinct from the two
+  internal factors A and B of `K9-SPLIT`. Neither internal factor alone is
+  promoted to the census verdict; the promotion uses their proved exhaustive
+  union.
+
