+
+## Controls
+
+The charged control suite was replayed from the frozen inputs with Singular
+4.3.2, one thread in every threaded library, and per-call bounds. Its aggregate
+schema is `jc2.k4ray.controls-replay/v1`; status is `PASS`; total wall time is
+9.194617 seconds. A separate literal tame-automorphism control was then run
+through the same frozen-hash `guided_gb.py` path.
+
+| control | exact-Q result | wall | interpretation |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| charged K=7 pinned light | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, basis 1, dim -1, NF clean | 7.774979 s | reproduces the reported approximately 8-second kill |
+| charged K=4, b=3 | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, 61 rows | 0.015799 s | charged low-K empty calibration |
+| charged K=5, b=4 | `UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`, 137 rows | 0.114120 s | charged low-K empty calibration |
+| tame `h=y-x`, `beta=mu*x` | nonunit, dim 0, vector-space length 2 | 0.007878 s | a nonempty tame chart survives; exact `J=6*x*mu^2` varies |
+| genuine tame automorphism | nonunit, dim 0, vector-space length 1 | 0.008069 s | exact `J=1` point and polynomial inverse survive |
+| Hilbert-hint main run | accepted, dim 0, length 3640 | 1.015288 s | prediction and computed length agree |
+| perturbed hint | rejected despite computed length 3640 | same call | target mismatch is detected |
+
+For every unit control, `reduce(I,G)=0` and all required output markers are
+present. The tame control guards against a driver which labels every ideal
+unit; the perturbation guards against accepting a basis merely because a
+computed length exists. The controls artifact manifest contains 47 files and
+passes `sha256sum -c`. The controls summary SHA-256 is
+`c26c07d5a2e14ab3c6defe6e8db63a66e3835a04c5e1e45c4a82ae9d79fef8c6`.
+
+The charged `CTRL_TAME_K1` is a tame-form nonempty-chart control, not a
+polynomial automorphism: its displayed Jacobian varies. The additional literal
+control uses
+
+```text
+h=x,  beta=mu*y,  alpha=(2/3)*(x-x^3-3*mu*x*y),
+(f,g)=(x^2+2*mu*y,x),  J=-2*mu.
+```
+
+The exact-Q ideal `(-2*mu-1,mu*mu_inv-1)` has the single point
+`(mu,mu_inv)=(-1/2,-2)`. There `(f,g)=(x^2-y,x)`, `J=1`, with polynomial
+inverse `(u,v)->(v,v^2-u)`. The guided basis is clean and nonunit (basis size
+2, dimension 0, vector-space length 1); both generators reduce to zero, and
+both inverse compositions were checked symbolically. Its summary SHA-256 is
